WEBVTT

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.900
Are you a SMART fella,

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.933
or a FART smella?

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.433
Let's find OUT!

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.533
Here's one,

00:00:08.533 --> 00:00:09.967
a picture puzzle!

00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:12.333
Which shape completes the pattern?

00:00:12.333 --> 00:00:12.800
A.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.200
A filled square,

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:14.667
B.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:16.100
A filled circle,

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:16.567
C.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:17.967
A filled triangle,

00:00:17.967 --> 00:00:18.933
or D.

00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:20.333
An empty triangle?

00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:21.267
Five seconds!

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:28.267
TIME'S UP!

00:00:28.933 --> 00:00:30.100
The answer is...

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:30.467
C,

00:00:30.467 --> 00:00:31.633
a filled triangle!

00:00:31.633 --> 00:00:33.933
The rule is the shape gets

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:36.267
filled in but stays the same

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:36.633
shape,

00:00:36.633 --> 00:00:38.967
so the empty triangle becomes a

00:00:38.967 --> 00:00:39.733
filled triangle.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.467
Alright,

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.233
a word analogy!

00:00:43.233 --> 00:00:45.567
Sugar is to sweet,

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.900
as lemon is to...

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:48.500
what?

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:49.067
A.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:49.667
Yellow,

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:50.233
B.

00:00:50.233 --> 00:00:50.833
Fruit,

00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:51.400
C.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:51.967
Juice,

00:00:51.967 --> 00:00:53.167
or D.

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:53.733
Sour?

00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:54.900
Five seconds!

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:01.900
TIME'S UP!

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:03.000
It's...

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:03.467
D,

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:03.900
sour!

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:05.233
Sugar tastes sweet,

00:01:05.233 --> 00:01:07.467
so a lemon tastes sour.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:10.100
It is the taste each food

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.433
is known for.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.267
Okay,

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.300
a number series!

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:15.967
Two,

00:01:15.967 --> 00:01:16.633
four,

00:01:16.633 --> 00:01:17.300
seven,

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:17.967
eleven,

00:01:17.967 --> 00:01:18.633
sixteen,

00:01:18.633 --> 00:01:20.000
and then...

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.000
what comes next?

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:22.667
A.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:23.367
Twenty-one,

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:24.033
B.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:24.700
Twenty,

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:25.367
C.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:26.033
Twenty-three,

00:01:26.033 --> 00:01:27.400
or D.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.067
Twenty-two?

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:29.400
Five seconds!

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.400
TIME'S UP!

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:38.867
The answer is...

00:01:38.867 --> 00:01:39.467
D,

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:40.067
twenty-two!

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:43.033
The gaps grow by one:

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.233
plus two,

00:01:44.233 --> 00:01:44.833
three,

00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:45.433
four,

00:01:45.433 --> 00:01:46.033
five,

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:47.800
then plus six.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.400
So sixteen plus six is twenty-two.

00:01:52.533 --> 00:01:53.133
Okay,

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:54.967
a picture puzzle!

00:01:54.967 --> 00:01:58.600
Where does the dot move next?

00:01:58.600 --> 00:01:59.200
A.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:01:59.800
Top-right,

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:00.400
B.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.000
Center,

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:01.633
C.

00:02:01.633 --> 00:02:02.233
Bottom-right,

00:02:02.233 --> 00:02:03.433
or D.

00:02:03.433 --> 00:02:04.033
Bottom-left?

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.267
Five seconds!

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:12.233
TIME'S UP!

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.500
The answer is...

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.033
D,

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:15.533
bottom-left!

00:02:15.533 --> 00:02:18.200
The dot steps clockwise corner

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.267
to corner:

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:19.800
top-left,

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:20.300
top-right,

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:20.833
bottom-right,

00:02:20.833 --> 00:02:24.033
so the next corner is bottom-left.

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:25.867
Alright!

00:02:25.867 --> 00:02:29.300
Which one does NOT belong?

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:29.967
A.

00:02:29.967 --> 00:02:30.667
Sun,

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:31.367
B.

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:32.033
Jupiter,

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:32.733
C.

00:02:32.733 --> 00:02:33.400
Mars,

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.800
or D.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:35.467
Venus?

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:36.833
Five seconds!

00:02:42.633 --> 00:02:43.833
TIME'S UP!

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:45.000
It's...

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:45.467
A,

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:45.967
sun!

00:02:45.967 --> 00:02:46.433
Jupiter,

00:02:46.433 --> 00:02:46.933
Mars,

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:49.333
and Venus are all planets.

00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:51.767
The sun is a star,

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:54.167
so it does not belong.

00:02:55.333 --> 00:02:56.567
Here's one,

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:58.400
a number series!

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.033
Two,

00:02:59.033 --> 00:02:59.633
five,

00:02:59.633 --> 00:03:00.267
seven,

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:00.867
twelve,

00:03:00.867 --> 00:03:01.500
nineteen,

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:02.733
and then...

00:03:02.733 --> 00:03:04.567
what comes next?

00:03:04.567 --> 00:03:05.167
A.

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:05.800
Thirty-one,

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:06.400
B.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.033
Twenty-six,

00:03:07.033 --> 00:03:07.633
C.

00:03:07.633 --> 00:03:08.267
Twenty-four,

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:09.500
or D.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.100
Thirty-eight?

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.333
Five seconds!

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:18.333
TIME'S UP!

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.200
The answer is...

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:20.600
A,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.000
thirty-one!

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.400
Add the two numbers before it:

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.400
twelve plus nineteen is thirty-one.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.800
Each number is the sum of

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.400
the two before it.

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:31.567
Here's one,

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:33.100
a shape puzzle!

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.133
Which shape comes next?

00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:35.633
A.

00:03:35.633 --> 00:03:36.633
A circle,

00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:37.167
B.

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:38.167
A hexagon,

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:38.667
C.

00:03:38.667 --> 00:03:39.700
A heptagon,

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:40.700
or D.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:41.700
An octagon?

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:42.733
Five seconds!

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:49.700
TIME'S UP!

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:51.967
The answer is...

00:03:51.967 --> 00:03:52.500
C,

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.533
a heptagon!

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:56.733
The sides count up by one:

00:03:56.733 --> 00:03:57.767
square four,

00:03:57.767 --> 00:03:58.833
pentagon five,

00:03:58.833 --> 00:03:59.900
hexagon six,

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.067
so next is the heptagon with

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:04.133
seven sides.

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:05.833
Alright,

00:04:05.833 --> 00:04:07.567
a number analogy!

00:04:07.567 --> 00:04:09.300
One makes five,

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.033
two makes seven,

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:12.767
three makes nine,

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:14.500
so four makes...

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:15.067
what?

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:15.667
A.

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:16.233
Ten,

00:04:16.233 --> 00:04:16.800
B.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:17.400
Twelve,

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:17.967
C.

00:04:17.967 --> 00:04:18.533
Eleven,

00:04:18.533 --> 00:04:19.700
or D.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:20.267
Thirteen?

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:21.433
Five seconds!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.400
TIME'S UP!

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:29.500
It's...

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:29.967
C,

00:04:29.967 --> 00:04:30.400
eleven!

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.033
Each number is doubled then add

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:33.500
three:

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.700
four times two is eight,

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:37.467
plus three is eleven.

00:04:38.633 --> 00:04:40.067
Check this out,

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:41.967
fill in the blank!

00:04:41.967 --> 00:04:44.367
After the long dry summer,

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:47.233
the once green field looked completely

00:04:47.233 --> 00:04:50.100
blank with no plants left at

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:50.567
all.

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:51.067
A.

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:51.533
Crowded,

00:04:51.533 --> 00:04:52.000
B.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:52.500
Barren,

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:52.967
C.

00:04:52.967 --> 00:04:53.433
Frozen,

00:04:53.433 --> 00:04:54.400
or D.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:54.867
Cheerful?

00:04:54.867 --> 00:04:55.833
Five seconds!

00:05:01.633 --> 00:05:02.833
TIME'S UP!

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:03.967
It's...

00:05:03.967 --> 00:05:04.433
B,

00:05:04.433 --> 00:05:04.900
barren!

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.733
With no plants left after a

00:05:07.733 --> 00:05:08.667
dry summer,

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:11.467
the field is bare and empty.

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:14.300
Barren means nothing can grow there.

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:16.533
Here's one,

00:05:16.533 --> 00:05:18.167
a number puzzle,

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:19.800
and it's sneaky!

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:23.033
If five plus three makes seven,

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:25.733
four plus two makes two,

00:05:25.733 --> 00:05:28.433
six plus two makes four,

00:05:28.433 --> 00:05:31.133
then five plus four makes...

00:05:31.133 --> 00:05:31.667
what?

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:32.233
A.

00:05:32.233 --> 00:05:32.767
Eleven,

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:33.300
B.

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:33.833
Nine,

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:34.400
C.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:34.933
Twenty,

00:05:34.933 --> 00:05:36.000
or D.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:36.533
One?

00:05:36.533 --> 00:05:37.633
Five seconds!

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:44.600
TIME'S UP!

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:46.733
The answer is...

00:05:46.733 --> 00:05:47.200
A,

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:47.700
eleven!

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.633
Multiply the two numbers,

00:05:49.633 --> 00:05:51.600
then subtract them both:

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.033
five times four is twenty,

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:56.933
minus five minus four leaves eleven.

00:05:58.100 --> 00:05:58.500
So,

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.533
are you smart or fart?

00:06:00.533 --> 00:06:02.967
Count up your correct answers to

00:06:02.967 --> 00:06:04.167
find your rank!

00:06:05.333 --> 00:06:05.700
So,

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.133
how did you do?

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.600
Comment your score below,

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.067
and subscribe for more!
